{"kind":"report","text":"Exact-head review of 69734d4e465ba4b47e7d8286b84a00d884b129fc, resting on all 71 artifacts, packages/client/README.md first. Changes requested.\n\nArchitecture: the schema migration fixes E5.2. Config and journal writes now name schema 2; old value/path-only intents are explicitly decoded, return or recover the original receipt, and print manual local steps instead of inventing ownership. Older workspace mappings and markers are preserved conservatively, unknown versions fail before sending, and schema-1 migration is atomic at the config write. The new workspace reservation and grant lease check fix the originally demonstrated delay at workspace-token. They do not yet cover the whole asynchronous command or ownership of a shared repository credential.\n\nP2 — reserve before the earlier awaits too (packages/cli/src/main.ts:619–633). The command awaits open(ctx) and held(api,...) before bumping workspaceRev. An older command delayed at either step can therefore reserve after a newer command has completed and treat itself as the newer owner. An independent HTTP diagnostic held the response of X's GET /lanes/X, then claimed Y and installed Y's workspace in the same repository. Releasing X's older read let X return success and overwrite Y's remote and credential, while Y stayed selected and its saved mapping stayed unchanged. Both leases remain valid, so the remote authority checks correctly permit X; the missing protection is local intent ordering. Establish the command's installation reservation before its first await, capture its intended Room/lane/repository, and require that ownership to remain current through the final installation. Cover connection/session and held-lane read delays, not only the workspace-token response.\n\nP2 — fence the shared credential destination across Rooms (packages/cli/src/main.ts:628,645; src/git.ts:46–60). workspaceRev/workspaceBy are stored per Room, while all Rooms targeting a repository write the same artroom remote and .git/artroom/credentials file. A reservation in Room A therefore cannot see that Room B installed a newer workspace there. A second independent HTTP diagnostic delayed A's token response after its reservation, logged into B using the same home, claimed B's lane and installed B's workspace in the same Git repository. Releasing A's response returned success and overwrote B's remote and credential while the current Room stayed B. Keep ownership at the actual shared installation destination, with Room and lane identity, and compare that owner before changing any remote, file or mapping. Preserve concurrent work in unrelated repositories. Include both Rooms and delayed responses in coverage.\n\nSecurity: credentials remain registered for output redaction and written in private files rather than argv. Release deletes only its proven installation, and legacy migration does not delete a possibly newer credential. I independently changed the HTTP workspace-token response's leaseGeneration to a different valid number: the final check refused installation, printed Did not install, and left the credential absent. This supplies coverage the request notes its fake Room alone cannot generate. The remaining races install a valid credential for the wrong locally selected context, risking work being pushed to the wrong fork; fix destination ownership rather than loosening remote checks.\n\nSimplification: schema 2 and conservative manual recovery are clear and avoid replaying an act to learn its result. Use one installation-owner mechanism shared by workspace setup and release, established at command start and keyed to what they actually change. Do not add separate partial fences at individual network responses.\n\nValidation: clean root strict type check; all 86 client Node tests, two client workerd tests, 69 CLI tests, 66 MCP Node tests and one MCP workerd test passed. CLI bundle built (946.1 KiB), the built CLI entry's help passed, and four package dry-runs passed. All six changed artifacts were read in full against E5; the other 65 artifacts, including the lockfile, are unchanged. Three independent diagnostics passed: the two remaining race reproductions and a positive mismatched-grant guard test. Diagnostics are saved outside the clean candidate worktree at /tmp/artroom-checker-E6-diagnostics/checker-v6-review.test.ts. No deployment or remote Git mutation was performed. The complete live Room/client/MCP integration and currently requested MCP contract evolution remain in scope.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dd2251513eeedf30a42c610d552abfa2172612d5","binding":"assigned","head":"69734d4e465ba4b47e7d8286b84a00d884b129fc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72b6618216c9bb3001a8c72224f99b02c41f1f0f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f934a98fa8efcc34c1695fee9b59e58568876e3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:acbe8e8f574bd7675f3c7d4093976268fea10d59","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}